---
import:
  - undying-tide-base
  - undying-tide-presentation
  - undying-tide-creatures
requires:
  - jellyfish-figure
description: Creature figures - the predators, gene fragments, plankton and the rift move as they live.
---

***implementation reqs***

- The twinkle of each :PlanktonCloud: speck is timed by a hash of the cloud's index, the speck's index and `tick`, never by the :RunSeed: generator.

- The shimmer band of :CombJelly:, :FlickerJelly: and :SplitJelly: is rendered as a 3D band mesh with additive blending (`THREE.AdditiveBlending`).

- :Implementation: drives the glTF skeletal animations of `public/models/anchovy.glb` (`Armature|Swim`), `public/models/sunfish.glb` (`Fish_Armature|Swimming_Normal`) and `public/models/anglerfish.glb` (`Fish_Armature|Swimming_Normal`) through `THREE.AnimationMixer` in `src/game/render/glb-loader.ts` (`updateGlbAnimation(object, seconds)`) from the simulation's `tick` (`tick / 60`) so they advance only while `tick` advances.
  - :UnitTests: of `src/game/render/glb-loader.ts`, `src/game/render/predator-figures.ts` and `src/game/render/level-figures.ts` assert that `installModel` creates a `THREE.AnimationMixer` when animation clips are present and `updateGlbAnimation` advances it to the given time in seconds, that `buildCombJelly` includes 3D meridian comb rows (`userData.kind = "comb-row"`) and inner canals (`userData.kind = "inner-canal"`), that `buildAnchovySchool`, `buildArrowWorm` and `buildSunfish` include sculpted fallback fin/tail meshes (`userData.kind = "fin"` or `"tail"`) alongside their `.glb` attachment (`userData.glbModel`), that `updateGeneFragment` sets non-zero `rotation.x` and `rotation.y` on the `gene-fragment-crystal` mesh over a 2 s (120-tick) cycle inside a 3D `THREE.SphereGeometry` halo, and that `buildRift` builds both an outer tilted `THREE.TorusGeometry` (`userData.kind = "rift-torus"`) and an inner tilted `THREE.TorusGeometry` (`userData.kind = "rift-inner-torus"`) with non-zero `rotation.x` or `rotation.y` around a lit `THREE.SphereGeometry` core (`userData.kind = "rift-core"`).

***functional specs***

# comb-jelly-shimmer
Every :CombJelly:, :FlickerJelly: and :SplitJelly: 3D figure in the scene shimmers: a 3D band of light a quarter of its diameter tall sweeps down its figure from top to bottom once every 0.8 s, clipped to its circle.
- The band is the palette's comb-jelly colour at 60% opacity, added to the figure's colours so it brightens them.
- Each one starts its sweep at a point of the cycle drawn from its `id`, so no two are in step.

# split-jelly-swell
A :SplitJelly: 3D figure in the scene swells to 105% of its drawn size and back once every 1 s, about its centre.
- Its circle stays radius 26.

# anchovy-tail-flick
Each anchovy 3D figure (`public/models/anchovy.glb`) of an :AnchovySchool: flicks its tail: its figure turns 10° to either side of its heading and back, 4 times a second, about its head.
- The anchovies of a school flick out of step, each one an eighth of the cycle behind the one before it.
- The figure faces the way the :AnchovySchool: sweeps.

# arrow-worm-lunge-wriggle
An :ArrowWorm: wriggles while it lunges: its figure, faced along the lunge, is drawn in 4 strips from head to tail, each shifted sideways by a wave of 3 px that runs from head to tail 5 times a second.
- In every other phase it is drawn straight, its quiver while aiming unchanged.
- Its circle stays radius 14.

# stinging-jelly-pulse-sway
A :StingingJelly: 3D bell in the scene pulses, narrowing to 90% of its width and lengthening to 110% of its height and back once every 1.0 s, and its 3D tentacle segments sway.
- Each segment is drawn shifted up to 4 px across the line of the tentacles, in a wave that runs from the bell to the last segment once every 1.5 s.
- Its bell and segment circles stay where they are, and their radii unchanged.

# gene-fragment-bob-glow
Each :GeneFragment: not yet collected bobs, spins in 3D and glows: its 3D octahedron crystal figure (`THREE.OctahedronGeometry` with `THREE.MeshStandardMaterial`, `userData.kind = "gene-fragment-crystal"`) is drawn up to 3 px above and below its position and rotates continuously around its `y` and `x` axes once every 2 s (120 ticks) in `updateGeneFragment`, inside a 3D halo sphere (`THREE.SphereGeometry`) of radius 20 in the palette's gene-fragment colour whose opacity rises from 30% to 70% and falls back on the same cycle.
- Each :GeneFragment: of a :Level: is a sixth of the cycle behind the one before it.
- Its circle stays at its position, radius 12.

# plankton-cloud-drift-twinkle
Each :PlanktonCloud: not yet used drifts and twinkles: its figure is drawn moving round a circle of 4 px about its position once every 5 s, with 6 specks of radius 1.5 px in the palette's plankton colour inside its circle.
- Each speck lights up and fades out over 0.4 s, at moments that look random, at least once every 2 s.
- The same `tick` always draws the same specks, and the twinkle changes no :RunSeed: draw.
- Its circle stays at its position, radius 30.

# rift-figure-swirl
The :Rift: 3D vortex figure (outer `THREE.TorusGeometry` ring `userData.kind = "rift-torus"` and inner `THREE.TorusGeometry` ring `userData.kind = "rift-inner-torus"`, both tilted in 3D with non-zero `rotation.x` and `rotation.y` around a lit `THREE.SphereGeometry` core `userData.kind = "rift-core"`) swirls about its centre in 3D: one turn every 8 s while closed, one turn every 2 s while open.
- An open :Rift: has a halo of radius 56 in the palette's open-rift colour, its opacity rising from 30% to 60% and back once every 1.2 s.
- When the :Rift: opens, its figure grows from 60% to its full size over 0.6 s, and a ring in the open-rift colour widens from 40 px to 80 px and fades out over the same 0.6 s.
- Its circle stays radius 40, and it can be entered from the tick it opens.

# faceless-predator-figures
No :Predator: 3D figure has a face: no eyes, no mouth, no smile, and no mark or mesh that reads as one.
- :CombJelly:, :FlickerJelly:, :SplitJelly: and :StingingJelly: (`public/models/stinging-jelly.glb` attached via `attachGlbModel` in `src/game/render/glb-loader.ts` with `userData.glbModel = "stinging-jelly.glb"`) are translucent lit 3D bodies (`THREE.MeshStandardMaterial`) in the palette's comb-jelly colour with 3D meridian comb rows (`userData.kind = "comb-row"`) and inner canals (`userData.kind = "inner-canal"`); the 3D tentacles or tube lines below them trail straight from the body and never curve into a mouth.
- No :StingingJelly: tentacle segment mesh has an eye dot.
- Each anchovy of an :AnchovySchool: (`public/models/anchovy.glb`, `userData.glbModel = "anchovy.glb"`), the :ArrowWorm: (`public/models/arrow-worm.glb`, `userData.glbModel = "arrow-worm.glb"`) and the :Sunfish: (`public/models/sunfish.glb`, `userData.glbModel = "sunfish.glb"`) attaches its `.glb` 3D model via `attachGlbModel` in `src/game/render/glb-loader.ts` (over a sculpted 3D lit fallback mesh of body, dorsal/pectoral fins `userData.kind = "fin"` and tail `userData.kind = "tail"`, with `updateGlbAnimation` advancing the loaded `.glb` skeletal animation clip from `tick / 60`) tinted in the palette's predator body colour, with any eye or face sub-mesh hidden or tinted uniformly in the body colour so no eye dot shows.
- Each 3D figure keeps its 3D Drift outline mesh in the palette's drift colour, its palette colours, its drawn size and its circle, and every animation above moves it as before.
